<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 3.780 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 3.780 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 3.780 billion pesos from the secondary market on Wednesday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    358 days   22.77 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    176 days   21.79 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     85 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     41 days</p>
<p>    600 million     36 days</p>
<p>    600 million     29 days</p>
<p>    700 million     19 days</p>
<p>    750 million	5 days</p>
<p>    180 million	1 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
